# Production environment for the Scandia SKU Decision Engine.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` on the VPS and fill in the real values:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   nano .env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored (see .gitignore). Never commit real keys.

# ─── Anthropic API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The AI panel (briefing summary + per-SKU recommendations) calls Claude
# Opus 4.7 (claude-opus-4-7) — the most capable Anthropic model.
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/.
# If left blank, the engine still classifies SKUs but the AI commentary
# falls back to deterministic prose.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ─── API auth (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When set, the /run-daily and /decisions/* endpoints require a Bearer token.
# Generate something random: `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Leave empty during initial setup; tighten later if you expose those endpoints.
ENGINE_API_TOKEN=

# ─── Nasdaq Data Link API (Public Company Intelligence module) ──────────────
# Required to fetch live fundamentals + daily market metrics for US-listed
# companies via Sharadar SF1 + DAILY datatables (engine/public/adapter.py).
#
# Where to get it:
#   1. Sign up at https://data.nasdaq.com (free account works for ticker search)
#   2. Subscribe to "Sharadar Equities Bundle" (~$49/mo) — required for SF1
#      fundamentals + DAILY market metrics. Without the subscription, search
#      works but financials return empty (the FE falls back to demo mode).
#   3. Copy the API key from https://data.nasdaq.com/account/profile → API Keys
#
# CRITICAL — server-side only:
#   · This key MUST stay in backend env (read via os.environ in adapter.py)
#   · NEVER inline in client-side TS/JS — every public-company API call goes
#     browser → /api/public/* → backend → Nasdaq, never browser → Nasdaq direct
#   · Rotate immediately if accidentally leaked (chat, screenshots, commits)
#
# Both names are accepted by the adapter; NASDAQ_API_KEY is the legacy short
# form, NASDAQ_DATA_LINK_API_KEY is the spec-aligned name.
NASDAQ_DATA_LINK_API_KEY=
# NASDAQ_API_KEY=  (legacy alias — adapter checks this if NASDAQ_DATA_LINK_API_KEY is empty)

# ─── Engine knobs (rarely changed) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# These mirror what `python -m engine serve --help` accepts. The Dockerfile
# already passes sensible defaults; values here only override if you uncomment.
# CORS_ORIGINS=https://scandiafood-sku.online,https://www.scandiafood-sku.online
